        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "J7 pin 9: NET0035; +3V3 symbol on that bus connection. J11 pin 3: NET0035 and +5V symbol on the same connection (sheet 1, page 1)."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "J6 (4-pin) carries GND, +5V, and two GPIOs (/PORTB1, /PORTB2), passed through from J1/J2."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "This directly shorts the M5Stack 3.3 V rail to the 5 V rail, which could overstress or damage the M5Stack and any connected circuitry.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic connects NET0035, shown on the M-BUS +3V3 connection, to +5V at J11 pin 3. This shorts the 3.3 V and 5 V rails, contrary to the specified PortB breakout."
}

